Notices
========

This skill is original work (2026, NakhulGithesh), built from the workflow described in the video
"How to Make Money Clipping GTA 6 Videos (Turned Into A Free Skill)" by Jad M.H.

Third party components used at runtime, not vendored:

* ffmpeg (GPL/LGPL build) - decoding, rendering, loudness normalisation
* yt-dlp (Unlicense) - stream and audio downloads
* whisper.cpp (MIT) - local speech to text
* OpenCV (Apache 2.0) - face detection via the YuNet model
* YuNet face detector (MIT, opencv_zoo) - facecam detection, downloaded at setup
* Claude Code CLI (Anthropic) - optional scoring backend
* Any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint (LM Studio, llama.cpp server, Ollama /v1,
  vLLM, cloud API) - optional scoring backend via the openai route

The OpenShorts project (MIT, Copyright 2024 OpenShorts) informed the webcam-inset detection
approach: a composited camera is found by locating a small, off-centre face anchored to a corner.
That project is not included in this repository.
